      "claim_excerpt": "## Result\n\n**Scoped written proof with exact finite checks. \u03ba is unchanged.** This is about the one ordinary-BIT bootstrap stage of the current selected record #4470 (\u03ba = 60403/20000000). That stage is the delayed-cover producer of uniform rank `N = 2^H1`, `H1 = 25986965159937`. It is stopped at atom `w = ceil(e^(1/250))` with old ordinary leaves and has ordinary saving 0.0034363538396. Its source reserve (DELAYED-COVER-BRIDGE \u00a78, `BIT-ALLSIZE-PARAMETERS.json` `stock`) borrows `k = D(N^2(w-1) + ceil(log_q(B|GL_N(F_q)|))) + ceil(log_q S_old) + 1` digits, with `D = floor(log_N ceil(e/w))`. The source requires `k < e/2` \"for sufficiently large e\".\n\nResults (`research/selected-bit-stage-stock-band`, PROOF.md):\n\n1. **Two-sided parent envelope:** `D\u00b7N\u00b2\u00b7w \u2264 k_par \u2264 D(N\u00b2w + ceil(log_q B))`. This holds for every N, every odd prime q and every B, e, w \u2265 1.\n2. **Depth classification** for `N \u2265 64`:\n   - `D = 0` has no parent stock.\n   - **Every `D = 1` width overdraws the chunk** (`k_par > e`).\n   - Every width with `n \u2264 4N\u00b2` is infeasible.\n   - Every width with `n \u2265 16N\u00b2+1` fits (`k_par < e/4`, given `ceil(log_q B) \u2264 N\u00b2`). This includes all widths with `D \u2265 3`.\n3. **Selected bands**, with `t = log2 e`:\n   - `t \u2264 26091330481863`: no cover level runs.\n   - `26091330481866 \u2264 t \u2264 52182660963729`: the source prescription is **infeasible**. This holds for every B, q, S_old and every larger admissible depth.\n   - `t \u2265 52182660963735`: it fits, under two explicit hypotheses on `B` and on the old-leaf stock.\n\nSo the source's \"sufficiently large e\" begins inside a proved six-bit window of `log",
